Excerpts from netnews.rec.games.hack: 5-Apr-93 Re: What to do with a
wish? by Mark 'Mark' Sachs@psuvm. 
> I generally don't do that, as you can get a nice weapon by sacrificing at
> an altar. Just wait 'til you get a few wands of create monster and then
> you're set. :-)

Definately.  Unless you are so unfortunate as to not find an altar in
the Dungeons of Doom (which has happened to me, to my dismay), you can
easily get more artifacts than you know what to do with.  Also, I
usually manage to become the Hand of Elbereth/Envoy of Balance/whatever
it is for chaotics sometime in the game, which will give you a blessed
rustproof +1 artifact of your alignment (Excaliber, Vorpal Blade or
Stormbringer).  Also, if you're lawful, just go a-dunkin' those long
swords in fountains.  I have never had a problem acquiring a good weapon.

In addition, if you are a Samurai, don't wish for the Tsurugi of
Musasama...it'll muck up your quest, and you're going to get it anyway,
so why bother?

> Wish for ARMOR. I usually ask for a gray dragon scale mail first, then
> gauntlets of power (to throw Mjollnir, of course!) A shield of reflection
> may come in handy, or speed boots if you're not a character that gets
> intrinsic speed at some point. Don't forget to ask for armor that's blessed
> and rustproof/fireproof.

Definately armor for me too.  If you are fortunate enough to get a wish
early on (through a magic lamp, potion, fountain or what have you), get
that trusty suit of Grey Dragon Scale Mail.  You'll friggin' waltz
through the Gnome mines.  Since I always seem to find a co-aligned
unicorn in the mines, I just go to the bottom, nab that luckstone, lob
the various gems lying about in enourmous quantities at the unicorn and
I've got maxxed out luck.  I also manage to put together a decent set of
armor in the mines too (+1 or 2 iron shoes, +1 or 2 elven cloak, +1, 2
or 3 helm, a shield of some sort and usually leather gloves), and those
items added to your GDSM will make you pretty invulnerable for a while. 
All you need to do is find an altar, hang about, get a good weapon, and
the quest is yours.  From there, it is usually just an exercise in
patience to win the game.

> Friendly warning: If you get all the way to the castle without finding a
> scroll of genocide, use one of the wishes from the wand to get some. Genocide
> master liches. You'll thank me for this.

No, wish for a blessed scroll of genocide and wipe out all liches. 
That's much more fun.

